ears ago thanos erased half of the  population of the universe but the  people of this planet brought everyone  back with a snap of a finger  later dane whitman brings up a big  relevant question about the eternal's  involvement or lack thereof in those  events  why didn't you guys help fight thanos or  any war all the other terrible things  throughout history  cersei justifies the eternal's absence  by saying that humanity would never have  had a chance to develop if the super  beans had spent thousands of years  intervening in every crisis which makes  sense even though it's not a good look  even pepper potts suited up to fight  thanos among other references to recent  events in the mcu there's a news  broadcast about the movie's suspicious  earthquake and someone can be heard  speculating that it might have something  to do with the blip though it's happened  plenty of times in comics so far the  marvel and dc universes have yet to  collide on screen that lends some  significance to a couple of conspicuous  lines and eternals the first comes when  most of the eternals get together for a  feast in modern day australia with some  of the group catching up for the first  time in centuries when gilgamesh meets  kingo's documentarian friend he asks if  he serves the same function as alfred  and batman  don't eat up belle  i'll cancel the pizza  the second instance comes later in the  film as icarus visits chicago and the  human family of fastos when icarus meets  the son of fast those the boy remarks  that he's seen him in tv reports about  the deviance attacks and that he  recognizes him as a very specific  superhero dad that's superman with the  cape and you're shooting laser beams out  of your eyes  i don't wear a cape  now more than ever it seems safe to say  that most characters in the mcu know who  superman batman wonder woman green  lantern and the rest are if only because  they've seen many of the same movies and  tv shows that we have what's your  superpower  